  <prompt>Keep "Assigned To *" access as a feature after the C9 fix removes the read-time membership term: build ONE server-side invariant owner that, for every access-conferring "Assigned *" lookup on a project, matter or work assignment, puts the named contact on the record's grant-access list at Collaborate (or shares the record to the contact's linked licensed systemuser, or grants the named organization), records that it did so, and never re-creates what an operator removed. Call it inline from every BFF write path that sets those columns, through a sync endpoint from an MDA form post-save call and from every client-side writer after its create, and from a scheduled reconciliation job.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer — BFF authorization write path, Dataverse schema, ADR-036 scheduled jobs, classic form web resources. Follow ADRs strictly; surface every ADR/spec conflict as a §6.5 path.</role>

  <goal>A single `AssignedAccessMaterializer` (name final at implementation) owns the invariant "each registry-listed Assigned subject on a root holds the owner-mandated access unless an operator declined it or a veto forbids it". Its outcomes are recorded in a provenance ledger. It is invoked inline by every BFF writer of those columns, by `POST /api/v1/external-access/assigned-access/sync` (called by an MDA form post-save web resource and by every client writer, such as the Create Matter wizard, after its create), and by a scheduled `IScheduledJob` that covers non-product writes, backfill, 141 link changes and Secure/Restricted transitions. Operator removal through Manage Access sticks. The ADR-034 / spec amendment is drafted as §6.5 path B and cited.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>WHY THIS EXISTS. C9 (session 26): on the SPA/Teams workforce plane a systemuser gets flat Read|Write|Create from ADR-034 membership matching, including `owningbusinessunit`. The owner's C9 rule (session27:9) is: a systemuser's Teams/SPA access = their Dataverse access; a contact's access = grants only, at the granted level. Task 036 (the C9 flag-gated swap) replaces the systemuser membership term with Dataverse's own answer. That removes the path by which an internal user named (through `systemuser.sprk_primarycontact`) in an "Assigned *" contact lookup reached the record on SPA. Contacts already get NOTHING from an Assigned field unless the contact (or its organization) holds a standing grant (`AccessibleRecordSetService.cs:1147-1175` standing term, `:1177-1249` org expansion). The owner, round 2 item 5: "The 'Assigned To *' auto grants were one of the core reasons for the UAC — this needs to continue being a feature." Q5: the Assigned contacts are automatically granted Collaborate by a function that ADDS the contact to the grant-access list, so an operator can remove it.

WHAT CONFERS TODAY (verified 2026-09-30).
- The access-conferring registry is `MembershipOptionsDefaults.CanonicalAccessConferringRegistry` (`Services/Ai/Membership/MembershipOptions.cs:300-372`).
  - Roots: `sprk_matter` :303-313 and `sprk_project` :314-324 (attorney1/2, paralegal1/2, assignedtoexternal, assignedtointernal = Contact; assignedlawfirm1/2 = Organization); `sprk_workassignment` :325-337 (adds `sprk_assignedlawfirmattorney1` and `sprk_assignedto`).
  - Children: `sprk_event` :338-351, `sprk_invoice` :352-360, `sprk_todo` :361-364, `sprk_analysis` :365-371. Only the three roots are ever composed for access (`CallerPrincipalResolver.cs:520-524`), so child entries confer nothing on any gate today — see escalation (f).
- Grants live in `sprk_externalrecordaccess`, keyed contact|organization × one typed root lookup (`src/solutions/SpaarkeCore/entities/sprk_externalrecordaccess/entity-schema.md:38-43`). It has NO source/provenance column. The audited upsert core is `GrantExternalAccessEndpoint.CreateGrantAsync` (`Api/ExternalAccess/GrantExternalAccessEndpoint.cs:186`). It applies `ExternalGrantLifecycle.DefaultExpiry` (+90 days, `Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ExternalGrantLifecycle.cs:160-171`) to an absent expiry. It upserts ONE row per (subject, root), so a later manual /grant lands on the SAME row as an auto grant.
- Revoke deactivates the row (`RevokeExternalAccessEndpoint.cs:80`, `:162` → `ExternalGrantLifecycle.DeactivateAsync` `:406`).
- POA shares to systemusers go through `InternalShareEndpoints.ShareAsync` (`:201-383`), using `RecordShareLevels` (`Services/Access/RecordShareLevels.cs:51-62`) and `EligibilityRefusal` (`:666`), and are removed by `UnshareAsync` (`:395`). A POA share has no row that can carry provenance.
- The `/api/v1/external-access` group (`Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalAccessEndpoints.cs:123-126`, routes mapped `:129-175`) carries `DelegationRuleFilter`. The filter finds the target record by a TYPE SWITCH over the handler's arguments (`Api/ExternalAccess/DelegationRuleFilter.cs:211-281`), and its default branch DENIES. A new route whose request type has no case is therefore refused for every caller — the filter "attached" but never reaching the request type.
- Share-cache invalidation keys on the CALLER's tenant claim: `ImpersonatedRootSetSource.InvalidateAsync(cache, caller, …)` (`Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ImpersonatedRootSetSource.cs:220-233`) derives the tenant from `CacheTenantFor(caller)` (`:200-203`), which returns "anonymous" for a null principal. A background job has no caller, so a job-context invalidation would silently remove a key nobody reads.
- Manage Access already shows Assigned contacts as grant CANDIDATES (`src/client/pcf/TrackingFieldTrio/index.ts:230-237` `CANDIDATE_ROLE_FIELDS`, fetched at `:713-740`). That list is a client hardcode that omits `sprk_assignedlawfirmattorney1` and `sprk_assignedto` on work assignments, so it disagrees with the server registry.

WHO WRITES THE ASSIGNED COLUMNS.
- MDA form edits: ADR-034 notes these are "exclusively maker-portal edits" (`.claude/adr/ADR-034-user-record-membership.md:41`).
- The Create Matter wizard writes client-side via `dataService.createRecord` (`src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateMatterWizard/matterService.ts:282-287`, `:335`).
- BFF `RecordCreationService` creates matters and projects with `CreateTimeFieldMapping`, which can copy Assigned columns from a source record (`Services/Office/RecordCreationService.cs:207`, `:297`, `:378`).
- The AI `UpdateRecordActionCore.UpdateAsync` PATCHes any field of any entity, app-only unless the Job B apply seam supplies an impersonated user (`Services/Ai/Nodes/ActionCore/UpdateRecordActionCore.cs:87-141`, PATCH at `:136`; its entity-set map lists `sprk_matter`/`sprk_project` at `:347-348`).
- The census in step 2 is authoritative, not this list.

TRIGGER MODEL. D-1: no plugins. `docs/architecture/DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md` §3 has ONE invariant owner called from L1 (inline BFF write), L3 (async fix-up) and L4 (scheduled reconciliation). The owner-named triggers are:
- L1: every BFF writer of the columns;
- a product-owned MDA form post-save call to the BFF, using the proven pattern `src/solutions/webresources/sprk_kpiassessment_quickcreate.js:150-215` (`addOnPostSave`) + `src/solutions/webresources/sprk_bff_auth.js` (MSAL silent SSO);
- L4: an ADR-036 job, using the canonical reference `Services/ExternalAccess/ExternalAccessReconciliationJob.cs` (paging, transactional chunks, claim/marker, fail-recorded, `AddScheduledJob` at `Infrastructure/DI/ExternalAccessModule.cs:371-372`).
L3 (service-endpoint → Service Bus → worker) is not built on master; this task does not introduce it (see notes).

THE RULES THAT SHAPE EACH OUTCOME (owner round 2, binding).
- Restricted = no contact-based access on ANY record; internal users are unaffected (item 3).
- Secure: only named, direct grants count for contacts, so an organization grant confers nothing on a secure record (item 3; `AccessibleRecordSetService.cs:1279-1290`).
- The No Access List applies to contacts everywhere, and to internal users on secure records (Q4; task 143 builds the internal check).
- A contact linked to a licensed systemuser is internal: MDA and Teams/SPA must agree (C9), so it gets a POA share, not a grant row.</background>
