  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">1. The notes file lists every registry column per root, verified live. It also lists the child-entity entries with their disposition per (f), and the complete writer census with file:line and trigger.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">2. Given an UNLINKED contact set in `sprk_assignedattorney1` on a non-secure, non-Restricted matter, when the sync runs, then exactly one active `sprk_externalrecordaccess` row exists at Collaborate with expiry = today + 90, and the ledger reads Granted with that source field.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">3. Given a contact linked (141) to an ELIGIBLE systemuser, when the sync runs, then that systemuser holds a POA share whose stored mask equals `RecordShareLevels` Collaborate, no grant row is created, and the ledger reads Shared. A contact linked to a systemuser refused only because `sprk_isexternal` is true receives a grant row instead. One linked to a disabled or non-person systemuser is Skipped(ineligible) with no write.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">4. `sprk_assignedlawfirm1` on a non-secure, non-Restricted root produces an organization grant (no contact) at Collaborate. On a Secure or a Restricted root it produces NO organization grant, and the ledger reads Skipped with the reason.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">5. On a Restricted root: no contact grant (Skipped(restricted)). A linked internal assignee still receives the POA share.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">6. On a Secure root: behaviour exactly matches the owner's answer to (a). If prompt: no grant or share is written, the ledger reads PendingConfirmation, Manage Access shows the subject as a suggestion naming its source field, Grant writes through the normal path and marks Adopted, and Dismiss marks Declined.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">7. A contact subject on the No Access List for the root (contact or org subject; record or referenced-org object) gets no grant (Skipped(no-access)). A linked internal assignee refused by task 143's check on a secure root gets no share. An unreadable deny list or flag set produces no write and a Skipped reason — never a grant.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">8. A subject already holding an active grant or share at an equal or higher level, or a later expiry, is untouched (zero writes), and the ledger reads CoveredByExisting.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">9. Operator removal sticks. After /revoke of an auto grant (or /unshare-user of an auto share), the ledger reads Declined. The same holds when the auto grant row is deactivated OUTSIDE the BFF, or the auto share is removed through the OOB MDA Share dialog: the next sync or job run records Declined instead of re-creating it. In every case a following form-save sync AND a following job run both make zero writes for that subject, and a manual /grant of the same subject afterwards still succeeds. Known causes are NOT Declined: an auto share removed by task 143's enforcer reads Skipped(no-access), and after that No Access entry is deactivated the next sync/job re-creates it; a grant lapsed by expiry follows (e).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">10. Per (b): clearing or changing the Assigned field revokes the previous subject's unmodified auto grant/share. It does NOT revoke when (i) another registry column on the root still names the subject, (ii) the entry is Adopted (a manual /grant or /share-user landed on it), or (iii) the entry is Declined.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">11. Idempotency: running the sync twice on an unchanged root performs zero Dataverse writes on the second run (asserted by test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">12. Sync endpoint authorization, tested THROUGH the real `/api/v1/external-access` filter pipeline (not by calling the handler directly). A caller WITH Write on the record reaches the handler and the materialization happens — this proves the new `DelegationRuleFilter` case resolves the sync request type (without it the default branch denies everyone). Without Write → 403 from the filter. An unknown record id → the same 403 (the filter answers before the handler, enumeration-safe; the handler never distinguishes it). Unauthenticated → 401. A body that carries subject ids is answered from the record's own columns, and the supplied ids are ignored (test). A read or write fault → ProblemDetails with a reason code and a message, never a bare 500.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">13. Every BFF writer in the census calls the materializer after its write commits (a test per writer asserting the call with the created/updated root). A materializer fault never fails the writer's own create/update.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">14. Every CLIENT writer in the census (the Create Matter wizard at minimum) calls the sync endpoint with the created record's type and id after its write succeeds (a component/service test per writer asserting the request). A failed sync call is logged and does not fail the wizard.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">15. The web resource fires on post-save of the project, matter and work assignment main forms. With `Spaarke.BffAuth` absent it logs and skips without breaking the form.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">16. The job covers the full root sweep, grant→share conversion when 141 links a contact (the grant is revoked, the share is created, and a Declined state carries over), out-of-band removal detection (criterion 9), Secure/Restricted transitions per (a), and renewal per (e). Paging past its ceiling reports TRUNCATED. A faulted scan records Success=false. Posture and cadence per (g). A share written or removed by the job invalidates the target user's root-set cache under the tenant key `ImpersonatedRootSetSource.GetAsync` reads (test asserts the key; "anonymous" fails the test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">17. Per (d): if the owner chooses retirement, the standing and org-expansion terms no longer contribute to the access composition (test: a standing contact named in no Assigned field and holding no grant loses the record), AND a pre-retirement backfill evidence table shows every subject they served holds an equal-or-higher materialized grant. If the owner chooses to keep them, removing an auto grant in Manage Access for a subject that still reaches the root through a standing or org-expansion term tells the operator so, naming the term, before and after the removal (test + UI evidence) — an operator is never shown "removed" while access silently remains.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">18. The ADR-034 full-ADR amendment and the spec/design amendment text are drafted, the §6.5 path-B block is in the PR description, and DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md §5 has the new invariant row naming this owner.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">19. Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in criteria 2-17 (link/unlinked/ineligible, org vs contact, Secure/Restricted/No-Access, covered, declined incl. out-of-band, adopted, multi-field same subject, idempotency, endpoint negatives through the filter, client writers, fault paths, conversion, cache key). Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the notes. No ADR-038-banned test shapes. No criterion is met by a test that only asserts a mock was called with arguments the test itself supplied.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">20. Build green; full BFF unit suite green; ArchTests green. Publish size reported as fresh-master vs fresh-branch absolute sizes, delta, zip tool and both file counts, all ≤ 60 MB. No new HIGH CVE. No new `.WithClientSecret`. `GrantMembershipAsync` has zero callers. No Dataverse plugin, flow or service endpoint registered.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">21. MANUAL live gate on spaarkedev1, run with the existing non-admin test users in their current BUs (no relocation), with the evidence recorded:
(i) setting an unlinked external contact as Assigned Attorney on a matter via the MDA form creates the Collaborate grant within the post-save call, and that contact then reaches the matter on the SPA;
(ii) for a linked internal test user who, BEFORE the save, cannot open the chosen root in MDA (recorded — pick a root outside that user's role-depth reach; if no such user/root pair exists without relocating a user, fire escalation instead of weakening the check), setting that user's contact creates the POA share, and that user then opens the root in BOTH MDA and Teams/SPA;
(iii) removing the grant in Manage Access, then re-saving the form AND letting one job run pass, does not re-create it;
(iv) clearing the field revokes an unmodified auto grant per (b);
(v) a root created through the Create Matter wizard with an Assigned Attorney has the grant immediately after the wizard finishes, before any job run.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Form post-save materializes the grant">
      <steps>
        <step>As a non-admin test user with Write on a non-secure matter, open it at https://{org}.crm.dynamics.com and set Assigned Attorney 1 to an unlinked external contact; save.</step>
        <step>Open Manage Access on the same form.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The contact appears in Current Access at Collaborate with an expiry 90 days out, and its provenance names the source field.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Removal sticks">
      <steps>
        <step>In Manage Access, remove the auto grant from the previous test and confirm.</step>
        <step>Edit any other field on the matter; save; reopen Manage Access.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The contact is not re-added. It remains grantable manually from the picker.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Secure suggestion (only if escalation (a) = prompt)">
      <steps>
        <step>On a provisioned secure project, set Assigned Paralegal 1 to a contact; save; open Manage Access.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The contact shows as a suggestion naming "Assigned Paralegal 1" with Grant / Dismiss. Nothing is granted until Grant is clicked.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="ADR-021 dark mode">
      <steps>
        <step>Switch the app to dark theme and open Manage Access with a suggestion row visible.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The suggestion row and its buttons use Fluent v9 semantic tokens, with no hardcoded light-theme colors.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <notes>Defect C9 (notes/session26-uac-defects-and-synopsis.md §C9) and owner round 2 items 3, 5 and Q1/Q5 (notes/session27-owner-decisions-and-research.md:16-37). Session-27 live fact: only 1 of 8 active interactive dev systemusers has sprk_primarycontact (session27:40), which is why 141 is a hard dependency. Coordination:
- task 064's report DTO has a "derived-from-field" provenance. Materialized auto grants are explicit grants with a source field, so 064/066 must show the source-field provenance from the ledger rather than re-derive it. Flag this to the orchestrator if 064 has not landed.
- task 087 (FR-32 append hooks) sees auto grants automatically, because they go through CreateGrantAsync.
- L3 (Dataverse service endpoint → Service Bus → BFF worker, DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md §3) is not built on master. If one exists at execution time, register this same materializer on it as a fourth trigger — the invariant owner stays one class.
- Residual window: a non-product write (grid edit, import, flow) waits for the next job tick. In the removal direction (revoke-on-change) that window is fail-OPEN, which escalation (g)'s cadence bounds once the job's revoke switch is on. State it in the PR.
- task 143's enforcer removes auto shares of walled users; this task records those as Skipped(no-access) (not Declined), so the Assigned invariant restores them when the wall is lifted. 143's own "removal is not reversible" rule covers MANUAL shares only.
- task 036 lists 142 as a hard dependency (036 POML deps + amendment 3): its flag must not be enabled until this task is live and its backfill has run.</notes>

