    <outcome date="2026-10-03" branch="task/uac-r2-142-r1" base="327bbbc59" round="r1 (adversarial verifier, 19 items)">
FIX ROUND r1. Full per-item record: notes/task-142-assigned-field-auto-grants.md section 11; seeds in section 5; new residuals R-10..R-12 in section 9; merge order G-0 in section 7. Live writes: none.

FIXED. (1, high; criteria 8/9) An expired grant no longer covers: FreshAsync and ContinueCoveredAsync count a row only when ExternalParticipationService.ConfersAccessOn(row.ExpiresDate, today) (the read filter's own predicate, via one private Conferring helper); a covering grant that is still there but LAPSED is a known cause (expiry, owner (e)/A5) and is decided fresh, so the still-assigned subject gets Collaborate again; a covering grant that was DEACTIVATED is still Declined. (2, medium; ADR-003) When rows exist on the key but none confers, the rule asks the grant core for an explicit DefaultExpiry(today) (today + 90, the renewal date; no conferring date to shorten), so the core no longer answers expired_not_restored there; a lapsed row's level is not a prior to restore. A Warning on the fresh path is now a failure (grant-not-conferring) with no ledger write; on the restore path the level is put back and the row is recorded Revoked(prior-level-restored-lapsed) with action ledger (no access was restored, none reported). New reason code AssignedAccessReason.PriorLevelRestoredLapsed (ledger schema doc updated).

TESTS ADDED (each guard seeded alone, watched fail, restored byte-for-byte and touched): P1 + expiring-today twin, P2 + deactivated twin, P3, the read race (GrantTable.BeforeGrantQuery test hook), the lapsed restore, (3) share kept while another registry column names the subject, (4) share with an operator-modified mask kept (widened / narrowed), (5) S5 share kept on a secure record, (6) R2 inactive organization = Skipped(subject-inactive) and restored on reactivation, (10) Restricted after Granted kept and not renewed, renewed once Standard again, (11) a disabled linked user keeps the share with zero writes. Seeds: S1 3, S2 1, S2b 1, S3 4, S4 1, S5 1, J 1, F 2, G 1, D 1, E 1; R (the materializer renewal guard alone) 0 because the grant core's task-138 Restricted refusal is a second layer, R2 (both layers) 1.

PROVEN WRONG / NOT CLOSABLE HERE. (9) Disproven: the wizard's create payload carries sprk_issecure = true (projectService.ts:281-286; projectService.test.ts:116-132) and IsSecure is that column alone (ExternalParticipationService.FlagsFrom), so the job sees a secure record from its first instant and suggests (A3); coordination kept as R-10 for round 2 item 2's future lock on sprk_issecure. (11) Link moves have no product path under the 141 contract (a link is never re-pointed or cleared, the column is FLS-locked to the BFF, a second link to a contact bound to another oid is refused) - R-11; the eligibility half is pinned. (7) Merge precondition: verified b38756ba6 is in task/uac-r2-133-b2(-r2) and 33108909e in task/uac-r2-137-b2, none of 133-b2-r2 / 137-b2 / 143-r2 is in work; merge order incl. the 137x143 semantic-conflict fix 843d62b46 is gate G-0 (main session). (8) ADR-034 A4 acceptance (G-9) and the PR description stay with the owner / main session.

