    <outcome date="2026-10-03" branch="task/uac-r2-142-r4" base="d48f5191e" round="r4 (owner round 13 items 4 and 5, BINDING)">
FIX ROUND r4. Base = task/uac-r2-142-r3 (d48f5191e). Full record: notes/task-142-assigned-field-auto-grants.md section 14 (R-13 in section 9 marked closed). Live writes: none. No escalation trigger fired.

ITEM 1 (owner round 13 item 4, R-13 fix now): the deny-veto check answers a TRI-STATE. IAccessibleRecordSetService.IsGranteeDeniedOnRecordAsync (bool) is REPLACED by CheckGranteeNoAccessAsync returning NoAccessCheckAnswer (Allowed / Denied / Unverifiable); the bool member is removed so no caller on another branch can keep absorbing faults silently (it fails to compile at integration instead). ResolveDenyVetoAsync returns a private DenyVetoResult(Denied, Unverifiable): an entry is Denied; a read fault is Unverifiable - memberships unreadable, referenced organizations unreadable, a fail-closed deny-list answer, a reader that returns no answer, any non-cancellation exception (an HttpClient timeout included, answered by the write-time check instead of thrown); a call without a record is Unverifiable too. The read path still removes Denied plus Unverifiable (composition unchanged, fail closed). Consumers, all fail closed (only Allowed grants or suggests): the grant core (task 139's CheckGrantAsync) maps Denied to 422 grantee_denied and Unverifiable (or an unknown answer, or a throw) to GranteeDenyListUnreadable, logged [EXT-GRANT] DENY-LIST-UNREADABLE; task 139's routes /grant and /invite-and-grant now REPORT the fault on the wire - GranteeDenyListUnreadable is its own decision, 503 sdap.access.grant.no_access_unverifiable, retryable, IsDenyListReadFault = true (the sibling of /share-user's no_access_unverifiable) - instead of the r3 wire (422 grantee_denied "or that list could not be checked"), and grantee_denied's detail now names an entry only; this changes task 139's tested route contract for the fault case only, per round 13 ("139 and 140 consume it"), and its tests were rewritten; the Manage Access modal shows its generic retryable failure for the new code (no client change). Task 140's callers: NONE exist on the work branch (git grep: CheckGrantAsync is called only by GrantExternalAccessEndpoint and InviteAndGrantExternalUserEndpoint, both task 139's; 140 POML pending, TASK-INDEX open); 140 inherits the tri-state through the shared core. The materializer's own call (secure suggestion) switches on the answer (Denied: Skipped no-access; otherwise not Allowed: DenyListFault + Skipped no-access-unverifiable, never suggested); its fresh-grant, renewal and restore paths branch on IsDenyListReadFault, which now carries every fault (a restore is never a green restore-pending for a fault). The job counts every deny-list-unreadable failure (unchanged mechanism) and goes red. Docs following the code: docs/architecture/uac-access-control.md, docs/guides/EXTERNAL-ACCESS-ADMIN-SETUP.md (new 503 row).

ITEM 2 (owner round 13 item 5): a task-143 wall-guard Unverifiable on the internal-user share path FAILS THE RUN like the deny-list fault. ContinueOursAsync (r3 :731-736, an auto share gone from a secure record) and FreshShareAsync (r3 :999-1003, a fresh or restoring share on a secure record) keep writing nothing (never Declined on a guess; a restore stays owed) and now call DenyListFault with the guard's fault name: an ERROR line tagged DENY-LIST-UNREADABLE, failure kind deny-list-unreadable (Complete false, sync 500 sync_incomplete), counted by the job (denyListUnreadable, Success=false). DenyListFault gained an optional detail argument.

ITEM 3: DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md row I-11 renumbered I-12 (master took I-11 at integration) and "Code on branch task/uac-r2-142 (2026-10-03)." dropped; the r0 outcome above now says I-12.

