ROUND 18 ITEM 1 (R-14, fix the cause): NoAccessListReader.GetDeniedRecordsAsync evaluates a subject set of ANY size. The deterministic pre-check (more than 25 organizations / 5 contacts -&gt; FailClosed without querying, ERROR "exceed the safe query bound") is removed. A new internal static ChunkSubjects splits the subject side into chunks of at most 5 contacts and 25 organizations (the systemuser in the first chunk; a within-bound set is one chunk with the unchanged filter); every subject chunk is queried against every object chunk and the rows fold into one accumulation (matches, provenance and subject kinds unioned). A null or a throw from ANY query still fails the whole answer closed, so consumers are unchanged (FailedClosed = Unverifiable everywhere). Effect: no permanent 503 for a grantee with a large wall set, no permanently red Assigned-To job, no read-path blackout for such a contact. Admin guide section 7.1 (the 503 no_access_unverifiable row): the limit sentence replaced.

ROUND 18 ITEM 2 = VERIFIER ITEMS 11 AND 12: AccessGrantModal's GRANT_POLICY_REASON_CODES gains sdap.access.grant.no_access_unverifiable (the server's own sentence instead of the generic "N failed. Please try again."), its comments corrected (the 503 details carry their own retry advice); TrackingFieldTrio bundle.js rebuilt with build:prod, differing from r0's only by that string, version 1.0.34 kept (never imported). notes/task-139-grant-model.md's deny-detail bullet is marked superseded by r4 and quotes the current 422 grantee_denied and 503 no_access_unverifiable details.

