  <amendments>
    <amendment n="R3" date="2026-09-30" source="owner round 3 (session27 note) — BINDING">(A1) Rule 5 governs: every Assigned-To auto-grant is Collaborate, with NO grantor-level cap (it still goes through 139's grant core with the explicit Collaborate ceiling, and never lowers an existing grant). (A2 REVERSED) Standing grants and organization access are NOT retired — they keep working on both planes; Assigned-To grants are ADDED alongside; escalation (d) is resolved "keep". (R3) Access must change within MINUTES: the form save calls the BFF so the grant/share is written immediately; add an "Update Access" ribbon command on project, matter and work-assignment forms that re-syncs that record on demand (follow the existing ribbon-command pattern; command enabled only for users with Write; shows the outcome); the reconciliation job is a safety net at an interval of 5 minutes or less (not hourly). (A7 REVERSED) Office quick-create defaults the internal Assigned-To field to the maker's contact (editable), coordinated with task 152 and word-add-in-r1.</amendment>
  </amendments>
  <amendments>
    <amendment n="UX" date="2026-10-01" source="owner round 3b UX + session27-ux-research (notes/session27-ux-research-ethical-wall-secure.md, disposition row 4)">ONE SHARED "Access" RIBBON GROUP. This task OWNS it.

Tasks 142 and 150 both add commands to the SAME three root-form ribbons (sprk_project, sprk_matter, sprk_workassignment main forms). There is ONE "Access" group, defined in ONE ribbon source file, with ONE command script. This task creates the group and its first command, "Update Access" (the R3 amendment's command). Task 150 later adds "Make Secure" and "Remove Secure" to the same group and the same script, rebasing on this task's work, never creating a second group or script.

THE RIBBON SOURCE.
- One authored file under `infrastructure/dataverse/ribbon/AccessRibbons/` (name final), applied to the three entities in one dedicated ribbon solution, per `.claude/skills/ribbon-edit/SKILL.md` (dedicated small solution, never SpaarkeCore).
- Where Dataverse needs a per-entity RibbonDiffXml, those per-entity copies are generated mechanically from the one authored definition, never hand-edited separately. Record the mechanism in the notes.
- In the Unified Interface command bar a ribbon Group does not render as a visual container. Realise "Access" as one FlyoutAnchor holding the commands as menu items (FORM precedent: the "Dark Mode" flyout `sprk.ThemeMenu.Project.Form.CustomAction` on `Mscrm.Form.sprk_project.MainTab.Actions.Controls._children`, `infrastructure/dataverse/ribbon/ThemeMenuRibbons/Other/Customizations.xml:28`, and its work-assignment twin at `:181`; the matter flyout at `MatterRibbons/Entities/sprk_Matter/RibbonDiff.xml:31` is on the homepage GRID, not the form), unless `docs/guides/RIBBON-WORKBENCH-HOW-TO-ADD-BUTTON.md` shows a better-rendering precedent. Record the choice.
- Place it in the form MainTab beside the existing commands (`Mscrm.Form.{entity}.MainTab.Actions.Controls._children`, as Push Updates uses at `ProjectRibbons/Entities/sprk_Project/RibbonDiff.xml:22` and `MatterRibbons/Entities/sprk_Matter/RibbonDiff.xml:18`).
- An enable rule on a control that never renders never fires (`docs/architecture/SPAARKE-SIDE-PANE-NAVIGATION.md`). Verify live that each menu item's enable rule evaluates, including on the first open after a cold cache (the cached rule returns a pending promise on a miss).
- When no menu item is available to the caller, hide the Access flyout itself rather than showing an empty menu.

THE WORK-ASSIGNMENT RIBBON IS NOT IN SOURCE CONTROL. `infrastructure/dataverse/ribbon/` has no exported sprk_workassignment entity ribbon: `WorkAssignmentRibbons/` holds only a merge snippet (`createtodo-button.xml`), and that form's Dark Mode flyout lives inside the separate `ThemeMenuRibbons` solution (`ThemeMenuRibbons/Other/Customizations.xml:181`). EXPORT the live sprk_workassignment form ribbon from Dataverse FIRST, check it in, and edit on top of it. The project and matter form commands are also split across several checked-in sources — Push Updates (`ProjectRibbons/Entities/sprk_Project/RibbonDiff.xml:21`, `MatterRibbons/Entities/sprk_Matter/RibbonDiff.xml:17`), the wizard buttons (`ProjectRibbons/customizations.xml:28-85`, `MatterRibbons/customizations.xml:29-137`), Create To Do (`ProjectRibbons/createtodo-button.xml`) and the project Dark Mode flyout (`ThemeMenuRibbons/Other/Customizations.xml:28`) — so build on a FRESH export of each form ribbon, not on any one checked-in file. BEFORE import, record from the live forms the list of commands on each command bar (expected, confirm live: project — Push Updates, Upload Documents, Summarize Files, Find Similar, Playbook Library, Create To Do, Dark Mode; matter — Push Updates, Create Project, Create Event, Create To Do, Upload Documents, Summarize Files, Find Similar, Playbook Library; work assignment — Create To Do, Dark Mode). AFTER import, every command on that list is still present and runs.

THE COMMAND SCRIPT. One web resource under `src/client/webresources/js/` (beside `sprk_fieldmapping_push.js` and `sprk_registrationribbon.js`; name final, e.g. `sprk_access_ribbon.js`, namespace `Spaarke.Access.Ribbon`).
- Enable rule "caller has Write on this record": a cached async rule (the `sprk_fieldmapping_push.js` `hasSourceProfile` sessionStorage pattern, `:165-184`) over `GET /api/v1/external-access/can-manage-access` (`RecordAccessGateEndpoint.cs:65`). It asks the server; it never guesses from a table privilege. Anything other than 200 with `canManageAccess = true` means "no" (hidden or disabled) — the route's own contract (`RecordAccessGateEndpoint.cs:68-73`).
- Authentication: reuse `Spaarke.BffAuth` (source `src/solutions/webresources/sprk_bff_auth.js`, web resource `sprk_/scripts/bff_auth.js`, `:4`) rather than embedding a third MSAL chain. Both existing ribbon scripts embed their own (`sprk_fieldmapping_push.js:874-900`, `sprk_registrationribbon.js:176-205`). Ribbon commands do not load form libraries, so list the helper ahead of this script in every CommandDefinition action and EnableRule that needs it (a preceding `JavaScriptFunction` on that library). `Spaarke.BffAuth.getToken` never opens a popup (`:173`, `:215`): when it returns no token the enable rule answers "no", and the Update Access click shows a "sign-in needed — reload and retry" message and makes no call. If silent sign-in proves insufficient for a ribbon click live, STOP and escalate rather than adding a popup chain. If the helper is absent, show a message and never break the form.
- Update Access action: ONE BFF call to this task's sync endpoint for that record. The handler runs task 143's record-scoped No Access enforcer (143 step 4, "for a record") and this task's materializer (which already consults 143's guard, so it never creates a walled share), and returns both outcomes in one response — 143 R3 amendment: "Update Access" also re-applies No Access. No second client call and no new endpoint (CLAUDE.md §11).
- Show the outcome the way the precedent does (`Xrm.App.addGlobalNotification`, `sprk_registrationribbon.js:271`): granted, revoked, skipped, shares removed by No Access, "not enforced" and "not enforceable" reports. A failure shows the ProblemDetails message (`Xrm.Navigation.openAlertDialog`, as at `:338`), never a generic error. Then refresh the form (`formContext.data.refresh(false)`, as at `:567`).

Constraints: ADR-006 permits this thin ribbon-command script (no UI component); no plugin (D-1); the server's `DelegationRuleFilter` stays the authority, and the enable rule is a convenience only.

JUSTIFICATION (CLAUDE.md §11) for the new ribbon source and script. Existing: `sprk_fieldmapping_push.js` (field-mapping push) and `sprk_registrationribbon.js` (registration) are the only BFF-calling ribbon scripts, each for an unrelated domain; no Access group exists on any form. Extension: neither can carry access commands without mixing domains; the new script instead extends the shared `Spaarke.BffAuth` helper's consumers and calls an endpoint this task already adds. Cost of doing nothing: the owner's R3 "Update Access" command has no surface, and task 150's Make Secure / Remove Secure would create a second group and script.

ADDITIONAL ACCEPTANCE (closed set):
- (a) the Access group, with Update Access, appears on all three main forms from the one source file and the one script;
- (b) Update Access is available to a Write-holder and unavailable to a Read-only user; that Read-only user calling the sync endpoint directly still gets 403 (the enable rule is not the gate);
- (c) Update Access writes the expected grant or share, removes a share a No Access entry forbids on a secure record, and shows both outcomes;
- (d) a BFF failure shows its ProblemDetails message; a missing token shows the sign-in message and makes no call;
- (e) every command recorded on the before-import list is present and runs after import, on all three forms;
- (f) the exported work-assignment ribbon is checked in.

ADDITIONAL UI TESTS (binding — part of this task's ui-tests):
- Update Access: as a non-admin Write-holder, set an Assigned field via a non-form path (grid edit), open the record, and run Access, then Update Access. Expected: the grant appears in Manage Access without waiting for the job, and the outcome notification names it.
- Update Access re-applies No Access: on a secure project where a walled systemuser still holds a share (added out of band), run Update Access. Expected: the share is gone from Manage Access and the notification reports it.
- Read-only user: on the same record, Update Access is hidden or disabled.
- Existing commands: every command on the before-import list renders and runs on the project, matter and work-assignment forms.</amendment>
  </amendments>
</task>
